The '''Mos Eisley prefect's office''',<ref name="Scum and Villainy" /> also known as the '''spaceport prefect's office''', was a [[law enforcement agency]] office built on [[Straight Street]] in the [[spaceport]] of [[Mos Eisley]] on the [[planet]] [[Tatooine]].<ref name="Complete Locations">[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']]</ref> In [[19 BBY|7958]] [[Coruscant reckoning calendar|C.R.C.]], [[Sedra Hoxin]] served as a [[Constable|police constable]] for the office and sent an [[Standard year|annual]] [[Life Day]] greeting card to [[Inspector]] [[Tanivos Exantor Divo|Tanivos Divo]] of the [[Coruscant Security Force]] with an update regarding [[Boba Fett]], leader of the [[Krayt's Claw]] [[bounty hunter]] gang, who were based out of Mos Eisley.<ref name="Scum and Villainy" /> In [[1 BBY]],<ref name="Date">{{FilmDate|IV|1|the appearance of the office}}</ref> two [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] [[stormtrooper]]s stood guard outside the building.<ref name="ANH">{{Film|IV}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
The Mos Eisley prefect's office first appeared in the [[1977]] [[original trilogy]] film, [[Star Wars: Episode IV A New Hope|''Star Wars'': Episode IV ''A New Hope'']].<ref name="ANH" /> It was first identified as the spaceport prefect's office in the new ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]] in the [[2016]] reference book [[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']],<ref name="Complete Locations" /> with further identification as the Mos Eisley prefect's office in the [[2018]] reference book ''[[Star Wars: Scum and Villainy: Case Files on the Galaxy's Most Notorious]]'', which was written by [[Pablo Hidalgo]].<ref name="Scum and Villainy" /> The name originated in the [[2004]] [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] reference book ''[[Inside the Worlds of Star Wars Trilogy]]'', which was written by [[James Luceno]].<ref name="Inside">''[[Inside the Worlds of Star Wars Trilogy]]''</ref>

